 Republican nominee remains a heavy favorite.", "watch": "Any rare West Virginia-specific polling or an extraordinary national shift against the GOP would be the first sign of a closer race.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "West Virginia is among the most Republican states in the country, with a partisan lean of roughly twenty points and presidential results that have drifted further right in each recent cycle. No candidate-specific polling or expert ratings are available for this open-seat contest, so the outlook rests on the state's underlying partisanship.\n\nThe national environment shows some signs of favoring Democrats after strong 2025 election results, and the president's approval is positive in only about ten states. Even so, West Virginia has proven resistant to national swings, and an open seat is unlikely to change that. The Republican nominee is a heavy favorite, with only a remote chance of a Democratic upset.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0132, "margin": -21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0389, "margin": -21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0348, "margin": -21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0377, "margin": -21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.036, "margin": -21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0348, "margin": -21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0374, "margin": -21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0384, "margin": -21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0335, "margin": -21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0352, "margin": -21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0348, "margin": -21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.046, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.05, "margin": -19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0391, "margin": -